- Continue passive-recon bug bounty analysis on the Spare program (phase POC, target api), producing structured findings per the 8-step analyst protocol and prioritizing the fleet-topology bypass as primary deliverable.

## Important Details
- Scope IN: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com. EXCLUDED: all other subdomains of both TLDs (e.g. api.us.sparelabs.com, metabase.sparelabs.com, api-staking, staging variants, ngrok tunnels are all OOS/dead).
- Passive-first: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation/data modification; write-POST probes only via AUTH_HELPED designations (engage routes).
- Facts vs hypotheses strictly separated; no classes on the REJECTED list; secrets referenced only via sha256 (e.g. regions body sha256 `fb9800acb09b65ec92591f4536e3ecfd08b8c3dba0d2ef9af3ed97047795c3fe`).
- Primary accepted finding: `/v1/global/regions` scheme-only Bearer bypass — `Authorization: Bearer x` → 200 + 725B region registry (7 regions: CA/US/US2/US3/JP/EU/UAT × {apiUrl, routingHost}; CA=in-scope, 6 OOS pairs), byte-stable 86–90h+, NOT patched; longcat "PATCHED" (2026-08-11) confirmed FALSE POSITIVE (only tested no-auth 400 path, missed Bearer-x vector).
- Ordinal finding context: multi-version envoy LB behind api.sparelabs.com — slow replica ~600–1500ms on fail-open routes vs 2–5ms on gated routes; confirmed flapping on several routes.
- Fleet parity: the {organizations,regions} bypass family reproduces identically on prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat.sparelabs.com (7 hosts); org-key + SSO data is prod-only (uat/us2/jp → 404).

