=== OAUTH STATE INJECTION FINDINGS ===

1. STATE REFLECTION: CONFIRMED
   - state param from POST body → reflected in WorkOS authorizationUrl
   - No validation on state content (alphanumeric, XSS, 1000+ chars all accepted)
   - Length: 0 chars (baseline) → N chars (with injected state)

2. redirectUri: NOT REFLECTED (stripped by backend)
   - AuthorizationUrl always uses server-configured redirect_uri
   - Attack cannot redirect OAuth code to attacker-controlled URL

3. CORS: FULL CREDENTIAL REFLECTION on SSO endpoint
   - ACAO: attacker origin + ACAC: true
   - Browser JS from evil.example.com can read auth URL with injected state

4. ATTACK SURFACE:
   - OAuth CSRF: Attacker can bind arbitrary state to victim SSO login
   - BUT: redirect_uri is fixed server-side → code always goes to platform.sparelabs.com
   - No token theft possible via state injection alone
   - Potential impact: session fixation if platform callback doesn't validate state ownership

5. SEVERITY ASSESSMENT:
   - Without state validation bypass → LOW (CSRF potential only)
   - With platform callback not validating state → MEDIUM (session fixation)
   - Current evidence: state injection confirmed, callback behavior unknown (SPA catch-all)
