## Objective
- Continue passive-first bug-bounty validation of the in-scope Spare surface (phase POC, target api), maintaining an evidence KB of stable accepted/rejected findings.
- Immediate goal: test OAuth parameter injection (redirectUri/state reflection) against the unauthenticated SSO-config oracle at `POST /v1/identity/workos/auth`, then document results.

## Important Details
- Scope IN: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com. OUT: all other subdomains (metabase.sparelabs.com, api.us.sparelabs.com, api.staging.*, forms.staging.*, admin-*.vercel.app, sparelabs.ca, ngrok tunnels) and all third parties.
- Passive-first: GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification; secrets only as sha256. Exception in practice: POST probes to `/v1/identity/workos/auth` and `/v1/public/engage/*` are part of the established accepted probe set (write-path validation, empty/safe payloads).
- Regions bypass body byte-stable 86h+, sha256 `fb9800acb09b65ec92591f4536e3ecfd08b8c3dba0d2ef9af3ed97047795c3fe` (725B, 7 regions: CA, US, US2, US3, JP, EU, UAT with apiUrl+routingHost each).
- longcat triage "PATCHED" for `/v1/global/regions` (2026-08-11) is a confirmed FALSE POSITIVE — it only tested no-auth (400), never the `Bearer x` vector; bypass remains unpatched.
- api.sparelabs.com sits behind a multi-version envoy LB: bypass/fail-open routes served by slow replicas (~600–1350ms) vs fast gated replicas (1–5ms). Singular `/v1/public/organization` flaps 2-way↔3-way (validation-leak-only); plural `/v1/public/organizations/{id}` is the stable 3-way oracle.
- Write methods on all bypass routes enforce 401 InvalidTokenError — bypasses are READ-ONLY (GET only). Engage POST paths reach the handler without auth (400/403/404, never 401).
- forms.sparelabs.com bundle `main.8a2a39cb.js` final state = PATCHED (zero sparelabs/atlassian/ngrok/metabase/vercel refs); an intermediate "REACTIVATED" entry (sha256 34f336cd…) was retracted as false positive. 3 Google Maps keys all referrer-restricted.
- Latest RISK scores: api 87, platform 68, routing 5, forms 12, web 15.

