## New findings from this run

1. **Auth bypass is ANY `Bearer` scheme** (not just `Bearer x`): empty bearer, null, undefined, lowercase — all 200 on `/v1/global/regions`. Basic/Token rejected. This means the middleware checks for Bearer prefix existence, not token validity.

2. **`/v1/global/organizations` is FULLY PUBLIC** — zero auth required (no header, empty header, any scheme — all 200). Plus full CORS with credentials (`ACAC: true` + `ACAO: evil.com`). This is stronger than previously documented.

3. **OATH hypothesis weakened**: `state` parameter IS URL-encoded by the server (prior summary was wrong — no unescaped reflection). `redirect_uri`, `login_hint`, and all other OAuth params are ignored by the handler. Only `domain` + `state` are accepted. `login_hint` causes state to become empty (interesting side effect).

4. **Org-scoped endpoints** (`/v1/organizations/{uuid}/*`): ALL 401 with catch-all auth gate — fake routes return the same response, so these are NOT real route enumeration.

5. **`engage/cases POST`**: Feature-flag gate blocks ALL 5 known orgs. Needs `organizationId` + `caseTypeId` (UUID) + `contactInfo`. Cannot proceed without a tenant with the flag enabled.

