## Objective
- Conduct passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation/data modification) security assessment of Spare's in-scope assets: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- Track confirmed findings for stability over time and identify new attack surface within scope constraints

## Important Details
- **Scope**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Exclusions**: ALL OTHER subdomains of sparelabs.com/spare.com; third-party services (metabase, ngrok, admin-*.vercel.app, sparelabs.ca, etc.)
- **Rules**: Passive-first only; sha256 hashes for any secrets; ≤1 rps; no account creation; secrets in commits use sha256 only
- **Multi-version envoy LB**: Behind api.sparelabs.com — fast replicas (4ms, ~0.11-0.14s) and slow replicas (500ms-1200ms) serve different auth logic versions; causes intermittent flapping across routes
- **Fleet topology**: 7 regional hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) confirmed via /v1/global/regions response body; routing.*.sparelabs.com inert envoy 404 everywhere
- **Longcat triage false positive**: Longcat claimed /v1/global/regions patched 2026-08-11 but only tested no-auth path (400); never tested Bearer-x bypass vector which still returns 200+725B
- **phase**: POC; **target**: api

