## Objective
- Conduct passive-first security reconnaissance on Spare's in-scope assets (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com) under a bug bounty program
- Maintain a rolling knowledge base of confirmed/rejected findings, tracking stability across multi-day monitoring windows

## Important Details
- Scope: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- Exclusions: ALL OTHER subdomains of sparelabs.com and spare.com; third-party services
- Passive-first: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- Secrets in commits: sha256 only, never raw
- Multi-version envoy LB confirmed — different replicas serve different code versions, causing intermittent flapping across many endpoints
- Longcat triage "PATCHED" claim (2026-08-11) on /v1/global/regions is a FALSE POSITIVE — only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x bypass vector (200+725B)
- Bypasses are now DETERMINISTIC (not probabilistic) — source-IP or route-based routing, not X-Forwarded-For
- Regions bypass on FAST replicas only; Organizations bypass on SLOW replicas only

