## Objective
- Passive security assessment of Spare's bug bounty program (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com) — identifying and tracking auth bypasses, IDORs, CORS misconfigs, and business logic flaws via read-only probes (≤1 rps, GET/HEAD preferred).

## Important Details
- **Scope**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Exclusions**: ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com/spare.com; third-party services
- **Rules**: passive-first only (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 for secrets
- **Phase**: POC (proof of concept collection)
- **Edge gateway**: api.sparelabs.com runs envoy on GCP (server: envoy, via: 1.1 google)
- **Multi-version envoy LB**: Fast replicas (~1-5ms) and slow replicas (~600-1200ms) run different app versions, causing deterministic auth bypass on different routes — this is NOT patching, it's a dual-surface from LB routing
- **longcat "PATCHED" false positive (2026-08-11)**: longcat triage claimed /v1/global/regions was patched, but only tested no-auth path (→400); never tested `Bearer x` bypass vector which remains 86h+ stable
- **Fleet-wide bypass parity**: 7 hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) all reproduce the bypass family
- **Known org UUIDs**: spare `d736519f-f384-4771-a2d2-4f95e884d790`, grt `1966c7f8-3e36-4320-b0d7-de0f7d8d4355`, dallas `e5f587ba-50e7-4b0c-a2e6-e01f061d048d`, winnipeg `6c84b370-5cc2-42c6-8cdd-146c99648535`, hsr (UUID from org-key oracle)
- **WorkOS SSO**: client_id `client_01F5KHYX32TCKB1E7YEAPE0H17`, environment_id `environment_01F5KHYX2HK6MTC68CHR2WGHCD`
- **GitHub repo scan**: scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs) — never produced code-surface data
- **Platform bundle**: `index-B6uSYXCi.js` (3MB) contains full OpenAPI spec of EAM/fixed-route admin API (170 paths) — all properly gated at 401/404

## Work State
### Completed
- **api.sparelabs.com/v1/global/regions**: Scheme-only Bearer bypass STABLE 86h+ — `Bearer x` → 200 + 725B region registry + ACAO:reflected + ACAC:true; body sha256 `fb9800acb09b65ec92591f4536e3ecfd08b8c3dba0d2ef9af3ed97047795c3fe` byte-stable; deterministic on fast replicas (8/8 → 200); OPTIONS 204 confirms write-method CORS chain; POST → 401 (read-only); body discloses 7 regions × {apiUrl, routingHost} incl. 6 OOS subdomains
