### New Discoveries This Session

1. **engage/cases POST — full validation chain mapped**: `organizationId` → `caseTypeId` → `contactInfo` → feature-flag gate (403). All 5 known orgs return 403 "External case creation is not enabled." Auth gate completely absent.

2. **engage/caseForms POST — different validation path**: `organizationId` → `formId` → `caseId` → `metadata` → form-ID lookup → 404 "Form was not found." **Does NOT discriminate org UUIDs** — goes straight to form lookup. Auth gate also absent.

3. **CORS uniformity confirmed**: Both engage endpoints return identical CORS to global endpoints — `access-control-allow-origin: https://evil.com` + `access-control-allow-credentials: true` + `Authorization` in allowed headers.

4. **No regression**: regions body, CSP leak, platform SPA — all unchanged.

### Assessment Status
The main open findings (regions bypass, organizations bypass, CORS misconfiguration) are stable and well-documented. The engage endpoints are feature-flag gated (not auth-gated), so they're not directly exploitable without the flag being enabled. Further progress on most vectors now requires AUTH_HELPED access.
