## Objective
- Passive reconnaissance and vulnerability assessment of Spare's in-scope infrastructure (`api.sparelabs.com`, `platform.sparelabs.com`, `forms.sparelabs.com`, `routing.sparelabs.com`, `spare.com`/`sparelabs.com`) for the bug bounty program
- Currently in POC phase targeting the API surface, with deterministic multi-version envoy LB replica-split creating dual authentication behavior

## Important Details
- **Scope IN**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope OUT**: ALL other subdomains, third-party services
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 only for secrets
- **Multi-version envoy LB**: Fast replicas (0.11–0.14s) and slow replicas (0.55–1.04s) serve different auth codebases; bypasses are deterministic based on which replica handles the request, NOT random flapping
- **longcat "PATCHED" (2026-08-11) is FALSE POSITIVE**: only tested no-auth path (400), never tested the actual `Bearer x` bypass vector
- **Fleet parity confirmed**: 7 hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) all exhibit identical bypass behavior; data exists only on prod
- **GitHub repo scan broken**: scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs), 0 files scanned across all sessions

