Interesting: the `formId` oracle is less discriminating than expected — all UUIDs return 404 "Form was not found" regardless of the `caseId` value. This means **the form existence check fires BEFORE the org/feature-flag check**, so without a valid `formId`, we never reach the 403 gate.

However, key method-awareness confirmed: **PUT/DELETE/PATCH** on `/engage/cases` require auth (401) while **POST** bypasses auth (400/403) — the middleware is method-aware.

