## Probe Results

**`/v1/global/organizations` (zero-header bypass):** Still `{"data":[]}` — 200 OK on slow replicas (0.75s). No new org UUIDs surfaced; empty payload persists after 86h+.

**`/v1/public/engage/cases` POST — all 5 org UUIDs: 403 Forbidden**

| Org | UUID | HTTP | Latency | Response |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| spare | d736519f-... | 403 | 773ms | `ForbiddenError: External case creation is not enabled for this organization` |
| grt | 1966c7f8-... | 403 | 332ms | same |
| dallas | e5f587ba-... | 403 | 361ms | same |
| winnipeg | 6c84b370-... | 403 | 216ms | same |
| hsr | 83303a6b-... | 403 | 318ms | same |

**What this confirms:**
- Auth gate is **absent** — handler runs validation + feature-flag check before any auth middleware
- All 5 known orgs have `externalCaseCreation` feature flag **disabled** (403 at the feature-flag layer, not auth layer)
- UUIDs are **valid** (invalid UUID would return 404 like nil-UUID does)
- Error body is **uniform** across all orgs — same message, same shape, distinct correlationIds
- Validation-before-auth is the consistent pipeline order across engage/cases

