**Key findings:**
- `/v1/public/organizations/{orgId}/{sub-resource}` is a **catch-all validation handler** — any sub-path returns 400 "not found" regardless of the sub-resource name
- **3 new gated routes discovered**: `/v1/analytics`, `/v1/dashboards`, `/v1/reports` (all 401, properly gated)
- **Universal CORS confirmed** on ALL `/v1/` routes including gated ones (ACAO:reflected + ACAC:true + all methods) — the CORS middleware runs before auth
- **Bearer-x bypass is SCOPED** to `/global/regions` and `/global/organizations` only — non-global routes return "Unrecognized token type"
- **api.us parity confirmed** for CORS chain

**No new exploitable endpoints.** The attack surface remains stable and well-characterized. The confirmed bypass routes (`/v1/global/regions`, `/v1/global/organizations`) and IDOR endpoints (`/v1/public/organizations/{id}`, `/v1/public/organizations/key/{key}`, `/v1/public/engage/cases POST`, `/v1/identity/workos/auth`) are the complete set of findings.

