## Objective
- Conduct passive security reconnaissance on the Spare bug bounty program (in-scope: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com)
- Identify confirmed vulnerabilities, track stability across sessions, and prioritize next investigation steps

## Important Details
- **Scope**: IN: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com. OUT: all other subdomains, third-party services
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, secrets in commits sha256 only
- **Infrastructure**: api.sparelabs.com runs behind envoy edge gateway with multi-version LB (fast replicas ~4ms, slow replicas ~600-1200ms). Bypasses are replica-dependent (deterministic: 8/8 fast replicas bypass regions, 8/8 slow replicas bypass organizations)
- **Fleet**: 7 hosts confirmed for bypass parity: prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat.sparelabs.com. Routing hosts (routing.*.sparelabs.com) all dead envoy 404
- **longcat "PATCHED" claim (2026-08-11)** is a FALSE POSITIVE — longcat only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x bypass vector; bypass remains 86h+ stable
- **forms.sparelabs.com bundle**: main.8a2a39cb.js was CONFIRMED PATCHED (zero infra refs), BUT main.63fe135c.js is a REGRESSION with hardcoded ngrok/Atlassian/Metabase refs
- **CA data residency concern**: forms.sparelabs.com bundle routes BOTH Production_CA and Production_US to api.us.sparelabs.com (PIPEDA implications)
- **Staging API**: api.staging.sparelabs.com + api.staging.us.sparelabs.com are live with different code version (regions=400 no bypass, workos/auth=401 no oracle, terms returns real URLs for all mobileAppId)

