## Round Summary (2026-08-18)

### Engage Cases POST — Auth Gate Absent CONFIRMED
The 403 is **purely a business-logic feature-flag**, NOT an auth gate:

| Org UUID | Response | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Spare (d736...) | 403 "External case creation is not enabled" | Org recognized, "Other" caseType exists, feature disabled |
| GRT (1966...) | 403 same | Same — org recognized with caseType, feature disabled |
| Dallas (91d3...) | 404 "Other was not found" | "Other" caseType not configured for this org |
| Winnipeg (68f4...) | 404 same | Same |
| nil UUID | 404 same | Org not resolved |
| Random UUID | 404 same | Same |

- **CORS reflected on 403**: `ACAC:true` + `ACAO:evil.example.com` confirmed on error responses
- **Preflight (OPTIONS)**: 204 — allows `POST`, `Authorization` + `Content-Type` headers
- **Validation pipeline depth**: caseType UUID `00000000-...-0001` resolved server-side to string `"Other"` — proves the handler fully parses the payload before checking the feature-flag

### Forms.sparelabs.com Bundle — Still REGRESSION
`main.63fe135c.js` (7.16MB) unchanged — ngrok, FIN-1093, Metabase, Production_CA→api.us.sparelabs.com all still present.

### Engage Form Schema — Progressive Discovery
- `/v1/public/engage/form` requires `organizationId` + `caseTypeKey` + `formKey`
- `/v1/public/engage/caseForms` requires `organizationId` + `formId` + `caseId`
- All formKey guesses return 404 — enumeration still blocked without prior knowledge

### Attack Scenario Assessment
The 403 from Spare/GRT means "External case creation" **exists but is disabled**. If any tenant enables it, an attacker could submit cases without authentication via CORS. Currently no org has it enabled among the 5 known tenants. **High confidence this is the intended submit flow** — the endpoint is designed for unauthenticated external case creation, gated per-tenant.
