Here's the summary of what we've done so far:

## spare-hunt — What We've Done

**Project:** 24/7 multi-model automated bug hunting for **Spare** (spare.com / sparelabs.com) under their bug bounty program.

### Infrastructure
- Set up a 5-model parallel hunting system (Big Pickle, Nemotron 3, Longcat, Ling 3, Laguna) running ~every 10 minutes
- Deep GitHub org scan of `sparelabs/` every 30 minutes
- Triage pipeline that validates leads with a second model + live passive probes
- Running since **2026-08-07**, with **284+ triage runs** and **620+ repo scans** committed

### Validated Findings (7 bugs accepted, all STABLE)

| # | Finding | CVSS | Asset |
|---|---------|------|-------|
| A1 | CORS reflect-any-origin + credentials on entire `/v1/**` (all methods + Authorization header) | **8.1 High** | api.sparelabs.com |
| A2 | Scheme-only auth bypass `/v1/global/regions` (725B region registry with garbage Bearer) | 5.3 Med | api.sparelabs.com |
| A3 | UUID enumeration oracle `/v1/public/organization` (400/404/200 differential) | 5.3 Med | api.sparelabs.com |
| A4 | `/v1/global/organizations` fail-open (200 + `{"data":[]}` + CORS, zero-header bypass) | 5.3 Med | api.sparelabs.com |
| A5 | `/v1/public/terms` data disclosure (live terms URLs, no auth) | 5.3 Med | api.sparelabs.com |
| A6 | CSP + MFE manifest infra leak (prod+staging admin Vercel apps, Metabase, cloud infra) | 3.1 Low | platform.sparelabs.com |
| A7 | JS bundle staging infra leak (staging/prod hosts, Atlassian, ngrok) | 3.1 Low | forms.sparelabs.com |

### Current Phase
State file shows `{"phase": "POC", "target": "api"}` — all hunters are in POC/verification mode reconfirming stable findings. The last triage run (`2026-08-18-12-21`) hit a server error.

### Known Hold Items (need AUTH_HELPED — valid test tokens)
- Write-method escalation on `/v1/global/organizations` (OPTIONS advertises PUT/PATCH/POST/DELETE)
- Engage portal IDOR (cross-tenant journey/booking read)
- `/v1/auth/token/superAdmin` role-check bypass
- SuperAdmin token-minting endpoint

**Reporting channel** is still TBD in `scope.yml`.
