## Objective
- Conduct passive reconnaissance and vulnerability analysis on Spare's in-scope assets (api.sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, spare.com, sparelabs.com)
- Identify, verify, and classify security findings through repeated passive probing cycles with evidence tracking

## Important Details
- **Scope (IN):** spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope (OUT):** ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com and spare.com; third-party services (metabase.*, admin-*.vercel.app, ngrok, atlassian)
- **Rules:** Passive-first only (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification). Secrets sha256 only. No raw secrets in commits.
- **Phase:** POC phase targeting `api` surface
- **Fleet topology:** api.sparelabs.com (prod CA), api.us.sparelabs.com (prod US), api.uat.sparelabs.com (staging), plus us2/us3/jp/eu/uat regional hosts; all behind envoy gateway + Google CDN
- **Multi-version LB:** envoy routes traffic to multiple backend replicas with different code versions; this causes flapping between bypass/non-bypass responses and is NOT a patch
- **Model used:** bigpickle (LLM agent model)

