## Objective
- Conduct passive security reconnaissance and analysis of the Spare bug bounty program across in-scope assets (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com)
- Identify, verify, and track vulnerabilities across multiple subdomains with stability/replica-split analysis over multi-day monitoring

## Important Details
- **Scope**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Exclusions**: ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com and spare.com; all third-party services
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 for secrets
- **Infrastructure**: api.sparelabs.com runs behind envoy gateway + multi-version LB (Google CDN); fast replicas (4-17ms) and slow replicas (500-1500ms) serve different code versions — source of 86h+ intermittent flapping
- **Fleet hosts**: prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat — 7 hosts confirmed; bypass routes are fleet-wide
- **Known working bypasses (86h+ stable)**: (1) `/v1/global/regions` scheme-only Bearer bypass (fast replicas), (2) `/v1/global/organizations` zero-header read-only bypass (slow replicas), (3) universal CORS credential reflection on all `/v1/**`
- **longcat "PATCHED" (2026-08-11) is a FALSE POSITIVE** — only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x bypass vector
- **Write methods POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE properly enforce 401 InvalidTokenError** on both bypass routes — bypasses are READ-ONLY GET only
- **Phase**: POC phase, targeting api surface
- **GitHub repo scan**: scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs), 0 files scanned — needs fix

