## Objective
- Conduct passive-first bug bounty reconnaissance and vulnerability assessment of Spare's in-scope assets (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com)
- Identify and track confirmed findings, rejected hypotheses, and next attack vectors across multi-day monitoring (2026-08-07 through 2026-08-18)

## Important Details
- **Scope IN**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope OUT**: ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com/spare.com, third-party services (metabase.sparelabs.com, admin-*.vercel.app, etc.)
- **Rules**: Passive-first only (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification); sha256 only for secrets
- **Edge gateway**: api.sparelabs.com runs envoy + Google CDN; multi-version envoy LB with fast (~2-17ms) and slow (~500-1500ms) replicas causes deterministic route-based splitting
- **Fleet hosts**: 7 total (prod/api.sparelabs.com, us, us2, us3, jp, eu, uat) — bypass routes are fleet-wide but data oracles (UUID, org-key, SSO) are prod/CA-specific only
- **Longcat triage false positive**: Claimed PATCHED on /v1/global/regions 2026-08-11 but only tested no-auth path (400), never tested the actual Bearer-x bypass vector (200+725B)
- **GitHub repo scan broken**: scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs), 0 files scanned across all sessions — needs clone target fix
- **Phase**: POC phase, target: api

