## Objective
- Conduct passive-first security assessment of Spare's in-scope assets (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com) for bug bounty program
- Maintain continuous monitoring of confirmed findings for stability/regression and identify new attack surface

## Important Details
- **Scope (IN):** spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope (OUT):** ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com and spare.com; third-party services (metabase.*, admin-*.vercel.app, etc.)
- **Rules:** Passive-first only (GET/HEAD ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 for secrets in commits
- **Phase:** POC (exploitation proof), target: api
- **Multi-version envoy LB:** api.sparelabs.com runs multiple backend replicas — fast replicas (2-17ms) vs slow replicas (500-1185ms) serve different code versions; this is the mechanism behind intermittent flapping behavior, NOT patches
- **Fleet topology:** 7 hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) all share bypass code; regions body contains 7 region entries including 6 OOS subdomains (api.{us,us2,us3,jp,eu,uat}.sparelabs.com + routing equivalents)
- **Body sha256 (regions):** `fb9800acb09b65ec92591f4536e3ecfd08b8c3dba0d2ef9af3ed97047795c3fe` — byte-stable across 86h+ and all fleet hosts
- **longcat triage "PATCHED" claim (2026-08-11) is a FALSE POSITIVE** — only tested no-auth path (400), never tested the actual Bearer-x bypass vector (200+725B)
- **GitHub repo scan broken:** scan-target misconfigured (gladiaio org instead of sparelabs), reposcan-raw/sparelabs dir empty — no code-surface intelligence available
