## Objective
- Continuously monitor and enumerate the in-scope Spare security attack surface (api.sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, spare.com/sparelabs.com) via passive recon and HTTP probes at ≤1 rps
- Validate, stability-check, and update a knowledge base of confirmed/rejected findings across ~11 days of monitoring (2026-08-07 through 2026-08-18)

## Important Details
- **Scope**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com; ALL other subdomains excluded
- **Rules**: GET/HEAD only (passive-first), ≤1 rps, no account creation, sha256 only for secrets, never raw
- **Phase**: POC (proof-of-concept on confirmed findings)
- **Envoy edge gateway**: api.sparelabs.com sits behind envoy + Google CDN; multi-version LB with fast (4-17ms) and slow (550-1185ms) replicas creates deterministic replica-split behavior
- **Fleet topology**: 7 hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) × {api,routing}.sparelabs.com confirmed fleet-parity for bypass code; data oracles (UUID/org-key/SSO) are prod-CA-specific only
- **longcat triage false positive (2026-08-11)**: Claimed /v1/global/regions PATCHED — disproven, longcat only tested no-auth path (400), never tested Bearer-x vector which still returns 200+725B

