## Objective
- Passive-only security assessment of Spare's in-scope assets (spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com) for bug bounty, focusing on api.sparelabs.com as the primary target.
- Track stability of confirmed findings over time, identify new surface, and pursue remaining hypotheses toward proof-of-concept.

## Important Details
- **Scope IN**: spare.com, sparelabs.com, platform.sparelabs.com, api.sparelabs.com, routing.sparelabs.com, forms.sparelabs.com
- **Scope OUT**: ALL other subdomains of sparelabs.com/spare.com; third-party services (metabase, Vercel admin apps, WorkOS, etc.)
- **Rules**: Passive-first only (GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 for secrets only
- **Phase**: POC targeting api (confirmed in `{"phase": "POC", "target": "api"}`)
- **Multi-version envoy LB** behind api.sparelabs.com splits traffic: fast replicas (4-17ms) serve newer code (auth enforced), slow replicas (500-1100ms) serve older code (auth bypassed). Deterministic routing (8/8 on each replica type). This is the mechanism behind intermittent findings, NOT patching.
- **longcat triage "PATCHED" claim (2026-08-11)** is a FALSE POSITIVE — longcat only tested no-auth path (400), never tested the actual Bearer-x bypass vector. Bypass remains 86h+ stable.
- **Fleet-wide**: 7 hosts (prod/us/us2/us3/jp/eu/uat) all have auth bypass code shared; data oracles (org-key, UUID, SSO) are CA/prod-specific only.

